WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.031 --> 00:00:02.333
- Are you a new parent?

00:00:02.333 --> 00:00:05.375
Are you wondering when life
is gonna get back to normal?

00:00:05.375 --> 00:00:08.671
Well, we've got some great
self-care tips for you.

00:00:08.671 --> 00:00:11.254
(upbeat music)

00:00:12.341 --> 00:00:13.887
- Checked out of the
hospital this morning.

00:00:13.887 --> 00:00:15.304
We just got back.

00:00:16.164 --> 00:00:18.974
You wanna come visit with all the kids?

00:00:18.974 --> 00:00:20.910
That sounds great.

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:23.803
Fantastic, we'll see you soon.

00:00:23.803 --> 00:00:25.864
- Mama, you spent 48 hours in labor.

00:00:25.864 --> 00:00:27.901
They can wait 48 hours to meet that baby

00:00:27.901 --> 00:00:28.895
if you want them to.

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:30.601
Let's see how this should've gone down.

00:00:30.601 --> 00:00:31.945
- Oh, you wanna come over.

00:00:31.945 --> 00:00:35.524
Um, we're actually not gonna
take visitors until next week.

00:00:35.524 --> 00:00:36.905
Okay, man, thanks.

00:00:36.905 --> 00:00:38.820
Appreciate it; alright,
we'll see you soon.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:41.403
(upbeat music)

00:00:42.759 --> 00:00:44.751
- You guys need any
help or anything or...?

00:00:44.751 --> 00:00:45.890
- No, I don't think so.

00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:46.906
- Yeah, we're good.

00:00:46.906 --> 00:00:47.987
- Yeah, we're doing it.

00:00:47.987 --> 00:00:50.977
- New parents should always
accept help when offered.

00:00:50.977 --> 00:00:52.849
I recommend keeping a list on your fridge

00:00:52.849 --> 00:00:54.647
of things that friends and family can do

00:00:54.647 --> 00:00:57.370
when they come over and give
you that empty offer to help.

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:59.772
Let's see how that should
play out in real life.

00:00:59.772 --> 00:01:01.483
- Actually, yes.

00:01:01.483 --> 00:01:03.118
We're out of milk and diapers.

00:01:03.118 --> 00:01:04.627
Can you go to the store
and get some please?

00:01:04.627 --> 00:01:06.943
- And the dishwasher is full,
if you can empty it out.

00:01:06.943 --> 00:01:08.419
Oh, the baby's new clothes
are just sprawled out

00:01:08.419 --> 00:01:09.970
all over the living room.

00:01:09.970 --> 00:01:10.901
What else; I don't wanna forget anything.

00:01:10.901 --> 00:01:11.851
- Diaper pail.

00:01:11.851 --> 00:01:14.434
(upbeat music)

00:01:17.239 --> 00:01:18.072
- Hey.

00:01:21.059 --> 00:01:22.319
- There is nothing more important

00:01:22.319 --> 00:01:23.910
than making friends with other parents.

00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:25.907
No matter how cool your
regular friends are,

00:01:25.907 --> 00:01:27.782
they live on a different
planet from you now.

00:01:27.782 --> 00:01:29.816
So, let's see what Shawn should've done.

00:01:29.816 --> 00:01:31.018
- Hey, how's it going?

00:01:31.018 --> 00:01:31.851
- Oh my God, man.

00:01:31.851 --> 00:01:33.395
Am I ever gonna sleep again?

00:01:33.395 --> 00:01:34.511
- Depends, how old is she?

00:01:34.511 --> 00:01:35.757
- She's two months.

00:01:35.757 --> 00:01:37.035
- Well, with my first,
she started sleeping

00:01:37.035 --> 00:01:38.946
about four to six months,
so you gotta a little time

00:01:38.946 --> 00:01:41.023
before the sleep starts,
but hang in there.

00:01:41.023 --> 00:01:43.606
(upbeat music)

00:01:46.554 --> 00:01:48.721
(yawning)

00:01:50.253 --> 00:01:52.287
- You and your partner
made this baby together.

00:01:52.287 --> 00:01:54.202
Try to remember each other's names.

00:01:54.202 --> 00:01:55.500
Can we see that again?

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:57.667
(yawning)

00:02:02.497 --> 00:02:03.330
- I love you.

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:04.304
- Te quiero.

00:02:04.304 --> 00:02:05.304
- Muchisimo.

00:02:06.222 --> 00:02:08.805
(upbeat music)

00:02:16.156 --> 00:02:17.421
- You're not truly a parent

00:02:17.421 --> 00:02:19.210
until some well-intentioned stranger

00:02:19.210 --> 00:02:20.997
tells you to sleep when the baby sleeps.

00:02:20.997 --> 00:02:22.708
And while that can be great advice,

00:02:22.708 --> 00:02:24.496
it's just not always doable.

00:02:24.496 --> 00:02:25.882
Here are some other options.

00:02:25.882 --> 00:02:27.303
You could do something you miss,

00:02:27.303 --> 00:02:30.530
like take a shower, binge watch a show,

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:34.304
spend some actual time with your spouse.

00:02:34.304 --> 00:02:37.028
(upbeat music)

00:02:37.028 --> 00:02:37.861
(baby crying)

00:02:37.861 --> 00:02:38.800
- Can you take her?

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:39.633
I can't handle it.

00:02:39.633 --> 00:02:40.938
- I can't take her right now.

00:02:40.938 --> 00:02:41.771
There's a headache.

00:02:41.771 --> 00:02:42.899
- I'm trying to get her to stop shrieking.

00:02:42.899 --> 00:02:43.916
Stop please.

00:02:43.916 --> 00:02:45.947
- It is hard enough
those first couple months

00:02:45.947 --> 00:02:48.188
if you guys are battling each
other every step of the way.

00:02:48.188 --> 00:02:50.685
Try to remember that you
made this thing together

00:02:50.685 --> 00:02:51.643
and you're a team.

00:02:51.643 --> 00:02:53.800
Let's see how dad could've done better.

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:55.509
- Oh my God, I can't, she's
been crying for over an hour.

00:02:55.509 --> 00:02:57.752
- Okay, okay, let's tag team this.

00:02:57.752 --> 00:03:00.273
You go outside; take ten,

00:03:00.273 --> 00:03:01.644
and I'll get her fed.

00:03:01.644 --> 00:03:04.206
(upbeat music)

00:03:04.206 --> 00:03:05.388
But you come back.

00:03:05.388 --> 00:03:07.638
You come back; ten minutes.

